A||N||2||DaveL||Constant Fan||||1||
Z||000000||DaveL||09-21-2000||03:51 PM||||I read a post where some one advised against setting up the rad fan to run all the time, saynig that it would make the engine run too cool and take forever to warm up. This aint so! As long as you haven't removed the thermostat, it will still warm up just as quick. My fan has been running constantly since I bought the car, and it has caused no problems. The fan died once, but they're really cheap and easy to replace. I also have a 180 degree thermostat. Only thing I have noticed is that the oil won't stay clean as long. Removing the thermostat would cause all sort of odd things.||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||09-21-2000||11:50 PM||||You're right - the thermostat keeps the engine at operating temperature, even if the fan runs all the time.<P>Ogre has stated more than once, that a full-time fan is <B>not</B> a bad thing, and I believe it. Well, okay, not <B>full-</B>time, maybe  - but at least when the ignition is on.<P>I had a "beater" FWD car would overheat occasionally in slow, stop-and-go situations.  Replacing the fan switch fixed it.<P>Much later, the replacement switch failed again (had to rescue it by turning the A/C on).  Didn't want to put <B>any</B> money into the car, so I just hooked the fan switch wire to a ground so it ran all the time (with key on).  Worked like a charm.<P>The only negatives I can think of a full-time fan are:<P> 1. More wear and tear on the fan motor (but they're tough),<P>  2. You can run the battery down faster, if you leave the ignition on, and<P>  3. Possibly slight reduction in gas mileage due to higher load from the alternator (detectable? - don't know)         <P>  ||||reg||14
Z||000002||Standard||09-22-2000||01:29 PM||||Just hook up a manual fan switch.  Then you can turn it on in stop and go traffic and turn it off when you get on the highway.  Takes about 15 minutes..  <P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
